-- title:
--   Naturality of level automorphisms on supersingular charts, q=3
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q=3$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number not divisible by $q$, and let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell\equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell\mid M'$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $q$ a non-unit of $A$, and let $W$ be a finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M'$ whose members are exactly the supersingular places `ssPlaces q M'` (rational, affine-geometric places at which $j$ evaluates into the supersingular $j$-set). Assume $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'\le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, and fix a constant reduction $R_0$ of the base-changed full modular function field whose residue map computes the coefficientwise reduction of Laurent series over $A$ (`hR₀`), an index $\zeta$ of primitive $q$-th roots of unity, and families of valuation subrings $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ indexed by $\mathbb{P}^1(\mathbb{Z}/q)$ and $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$ indexed by $W$. The hypotheses on these families are: $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ consists of the quotients of Laurent series with coefficients in $A$ whose denominator has nonzero reduction; each $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathfrak{l})$ is the pullback of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ along some `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ moving $\infty$ to $\mathfrak{l}$ under `redQ`; $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ is injective and is permuted by pullback along all `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}\,s$ meets $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ in $A$, is stable under pullback along all such level automorphisms, contains an element $t$ with $t-a$ a unit for every $a\in A$, and receives the $R_0$-integers regular away from the poles of $j$ with residue in $s$, compatibly with reduction and evaluation at $s$ (`hSS_over`). Furthermore let $\mathcal{C}$ be a `SemistableCovering q M' A W`, and assume: regular prolongations $R_{\mathrm{SS}}\,s$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ over $A$ with value field $\mathcal{C}.\mathrm{FSS}\,s$ whose integer rings are the $O_{\mathrm{SS}}\,s$ and which agree with the charts $\mathcal{C}.\mathrm{CSS}\,s$ in integers and residues; disc sets $\mathrm{discS}$ and coordinates $\mathrm{coordS}$ forming a `DiscFamily` for $R_{\mathrm{SS}}\,s$ over the complement of the nodes of $\mathcal{C}.\mathrm{CSS}\,s$, transported by semilinear automorphisms of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ that preserve $A$, induce the identity on its residue field, fix $j$ and preserve the integers and the $\mathcal{C}.\mathrm{xt}$-points (`htransS`); the domain of $\mathcal{C}.\mathrm{CSS}\,s$ is the union of the non-node discs, its place map sends each disc of a non-node $Q$ to $Q$ and is constant off the domain; and the node set and the disc sets are equivariant under the residue automorphisms `resAut` attached to the subgroup generated by the `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ`, $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$. The conclusion: for every index $\zeta$ and every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, setting $g$ to be the semilinear automorphism `SemilinearAut.ofAlgAut (levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹)`, and for every $s\in W$, there is an automorphism $\varphi$ of $\mathcal{C}.\mathrm{FSS}\,s$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ such that `InducesOnChart (𝒞.CSS s) g φ` holds — that is, $f$ lies in the integers of the chart if and only if $g\cdot f$ does, and the residue of $g\cdot f$ is $\varphi$ of the residue of $f$ — and such that the place map of the chart satisfies $\mathrm{placeMap}(g\cdot P)=\varphi\cdot \mathrm{placeMap}(P)$ for all $P$ in its domain.
--
--   This is the supersingular half of the naturality of the semistable covering of $X_{\Gamma_H(q^2M')}$ in the case $q=3$, where the extra rigidity hypothesis on $\ell$ compensates for the exceptional automorphisms of the supersingular elliptic curve in characteristic $3$. It feeds the assembly of the covering, being used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_semistableCovering_equivClauses_of_valuationSubrings_semistableModel_inertiaInfty_charted_of_eq_three_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_semistableCovering_equivClauses_of_valuationSubrings_semistableModel_inertiaInfty_charted_of_eq_three_of_dvd).
